#702 HIS EXIT - DISCOVERY READ (D 2022-03-28 .. 2024-12-31), levels tl. Exploratory: nothing here decides; the stop is the operator's call; the holdout is untouched.
source: trades_discovery_exits_tl.tsv.gz; rows read 130. POPULATION: the spec key's first breaks filled at orh5 under the registered stop (the width rule at the fill); every stop variant can only remove a trade (too_wide), never add one.
ARMS: p33_s3_t10 (registered: 1/3 at the close of session 3, breakeven, SMA10 trail) beside 25 his-exit arms <trigger>_p33_<trail>: trigger r2 = 1/3 at +2R (a gap open above it at the open; day 0 on the minutes), d3 / d5 = the close of session 3 / 5, c3 / c5 = whichever comes first; trail t10 / t20 fixed, tspd = SMA10 when ADR20(D) > 0.0479 (his 'faster stocks': the top tercile of the discovery C0 ADR distribution) else SMA20, td1 / td2 = at the partial, SMA10 when the close is more than 1 / 2 ADR20 above its SMA10 else SMA20. The trail is live only after the partial, filled at the next open.
STOPS: lod = the low of the day at the fill (registered); lod_cap05 = max(lod, fill - 0.5 ADR); lod_floor05 = min(lod, fill - 0.5 ADR); level_m05 = the breakout level (the pivot) - 0.5 ADR; base_low = the base's low; each skipped as too_wide beyond one ADR20. R = fill - that stop, so R is NOT comparable across stops: combos are ranked on mean_pnl_adr (P&L in ADR units), R and the tail beside.
A group is the MATURE walks only; month-block bootstrap (2,000 draws, seed 702) 95% interval on the mean R.

HEADLINE - per level, the registered row and the best three NEW arm x stop combos (ranked on C0 by mean_pnl_adr among the combos that kept >= 95% of the registered row's trades - the same population), on C0 and C1
